<title>GERMANY: West German May adjusted jobless rises 25,000.</title>
<headline>West German May adjusted jobless rises 25,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 May 97	  Apr 97	   May 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.960 mln     3.031 mln	2.683 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.042 mln     3.017 mln	2.763 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+25,000	 +7,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		 9.6 pct	9.8 pct	  8.7 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	129,129	 173,407	  222,714</p>
<p> Vacancies		   308,671	 314,788	  300,257</p>
<p>Change in number in work Mar 97	  Feb 97</p>
<p>				 +25,000	 -22,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
